    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d156">

                <pb facs="0257" n="153" sameAs="frus:frus1913/pg153"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 893.51/1337.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            American Ambassador to France.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1913-02-09">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 9, 1913</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Ascertain what information the Foreign Office has as to the status of the Chinese
                    loan question. Last reports indicate negotiations: at Peking are at a standstill
                    over the appointment of foreign advisers. This Government is willing to accept
                    the three nominations made by the Chinese Government, or appointees exclusively
                    from the lending powers, but considers an immediate settlement of first
                    importance.</p>
                <p>Repeat to London and Berlin.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Knox</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
